salvability:
中：adv. salvable的变形
英：n. The quality or condition of being salvable;
   salvableness.

sassed:
音标：/sæst/
中：v. 对…无礼, 粗鲁对待( sass的过去式和过去分词 )
英：v answer back in an impudent or insolent manner;

scantness:
中：n. scant的变形
英：n. The quality or condition of being scant; narrowness;
   smallness; insufficiency; scantiness.

sea language:
中：水手行话
英：The peculiar language or phraseology of seamen;
   sailor's cant.

semaphorical:
中：a. semaphore的变形
英：a. Of or pertaining to a semaphore, or semaphores;
   telegraphic.

sightliness:
中：n. sightly的变形
英：n. The state of being sightly; comeliness;
   conspicuousness.

slatternliness:
中：n. slatternly的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being slatternly;
   slovenliness; untidiness.

smegmatic:
中：[医] 包皮垢石
英：a. Being of the nature of soap; soapy; cleansing;
   detersive.

sogginess:
中：n. soggy的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being soggy; soddenness;
   wetness.

solacement:
中：n. 安慰；慰藉；安慰之物 (solace的变形)
英：n. The act of solacing, or the state of being solaced;
   also, that which solaces.

somnambulistic:
中：a. 梦行的, 梦游者的
英：a. Of or pertaining to a somnambulist or somnambulism;
   affected by somnambulism; appropriate to the state of a somnambulist.

sovereignly:
中：adv. sovereign的变形
英：adv. In a sovereign manner; in the highest degree;
   supremely.

spectroscopist:
中：n. 光谱学家
英：n. One who investigates by means of a spectroscope;
   one skilled in the use of the spectroscope.

starvedly:
中：adv. starved的变形
英：adv. In the condition of one starved or starving;
   parsimoniously.

stealthiness:
中：n. 隐匿性
英：n. The state, quality, or character of being stealthy;
   stealth.

sternforemost:
中：adv. 船尾向前地, 笨拙地
英：adv. With the stern, instead of the bow, in advance;
   hence, figuratively, in an awkward, blundering manner.

stipular:
音标：/'stipjulә/
中：a. 托叶的, 有托叶的, 生在托叶上的
英：a. Of or pertaining to stipules; resembling stipules;
   furnished with stipules; growing on stipules, or close to them;
   occupying the position of stipules; as, stipular glands and stipular
   tendrils.

subcoracoid:
中：[医] 喙突下的
英：a. Situated under the coracoid process of the scapula;
   as, the subcoracoid dislocation of the humerus.

subvaginal:
中：[医] 鞘下的; 阴道下的
英：a. Situated under or inside a sheath or vaginal membrane;
   as, the subvaginal, or subdural, spaces about the optic nerve.
